# Original Mac Pro SSDs (APPLE SSD SM...): turn the drive's volatile write cache off. With it on, a cache flush
# during heavy reads stops all I/O for 0.3-1.2 s (seconds with several), and the kernel sends one per fsync and
# journal commit. With it off the kernel sends no flushes. Installed by nodes/macpro/install.sh (component disk).
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="scsi_disk", ATTRS{vendor}=="ATA*", ATTRS{model}=="APPLE SSD SM*", ATTR{cache_type}="write through"
